6. User Manual 

6.1 Getting Started 

    -Accessing the Application:  

    -Open your web browser (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, or Edge) 

    -Navigate to the application URL provided by your institution 

    -You'll be directed to the login page 

Logging In:  

    -Enter your username and password 

    -Click the "Login" button 

6.2 Student Features 

6.2.1 Dashboard 

    -After logging in, you'll see your student dashboard 

    -View your enrolled classes, recent attendance 

    -Access quick links to check in, view messages, and check attendance history 

6.2.2 Checking In to Class 

    -Navigate to the "Classes" section or click "Check In" from the dashboard 

    -Select the class you're attending from your enrolled classes list 

    -Click the "Check In" button 

    -The system will automatically record your check-in time and location 

    -You'll see a confirmation message when check-in is successful 

    -Note: You can only be checked into one class at a time 

6.2.3 Checking Out of Class 

    -When class is over, go to your active session 

    -Click the "Check Out" button 

    -The system records your check-out time and calculates your attendance duration 

    -You'll receive a confirmation that you've successfully checked out 

6.2.4 Viewing Your Attendance 

    -Click "Attendance" in the navigation menu 

    -View a table showing all your attendance records 

    -See details including class name, date, check-in time, check-out time, and duration 

    -Filter by date range or specific class to find past attendance records 

6.2.5 Messaging 

    -Click "Messages" to access the chat feature 

    -View all your conversations with instructors 

    -Click on a conversation to see the full message history 

    -Type your message in the text box and click "Send" 

    -You can start a new conversation by selecting "New Message" and choosing an instructor 

6.3 Instructor Features 

6.3.1 Dashboard 

    -View all your classes, recent student activity, and attendance statistics 

    -Access quick links to manage classes, view rosters, and check messages 

6.3.2 Managing Classes 

    -Navigate to "Classes" in the menu 

    -Click "Create New Class" to add a class 

    -Fill in the class details: name, section, term, meeting times 

    -Click "Save" to create the class 

    -To edit a class, click the edit icon next to the class name 

    -To delete a class, click the delete icon (note: this will remove all associated data) 

6.3.3 Managing Enrollments 

    -Click on a class to view its details 

    -Go to the "Roster" tab to see all enrolled students 

    -Click "Add Student" to enroll new students in the class 

    -Search for students by name  

    -Select students and click "Enroll" 

    -To remove a student, click the remove icon next to their name 

6.3.4 Viewing Class Attendance 

    -Select a class from your classes list 

    -Click the "Attendance" tab 

    -View a table showing all attendance records for that class 

    -See which students are currently checked in 

6.3.5 Messaging Students 

    -Click "Messages" to access the chat feature 

    -Start a new conversation by clicking "New Message" 

    -Select one or more students to create individual or group conversations 

    -You can also message students directly from the class roster by clicking the message icon next to their name 

    -View conversation history and send messages as needed 

6.4 Administrator Features 

6.4.1 User Management 

    -Navigate to "User Management" in the admin menu 

    -View a list of all users (students, instructors, and other admins) 

    -Click "Add User" to create new accounts 

    -Fill in required information: username, email, password, and role 

    -Edit user information by clicking the edit icon 

    -Delete users by clicking the delete icon (use with caution) 

    -Reset passwords for users who have forgotten their credentials 

6.4.2 System Overview 

    -Access the admin dashboard to see system-wide statistics 

    -View total users, active classes, and attendance metrics 

    -Monitor system activity and usage patterns 

6.4.3 Managing All Classes 

    -View all classes across all instructors 

    -Edit or delete any class if needed 

    -Assign instructors to classes 

    -Manage enrollments across the entire system 

6.5 General Features 

6.5.1 Navigation Menu 

    -The navigation menu on the left (or top, depending on screen size) provides access to all features 

    -Menu options change based on your role:  

    -Students see: Dashboard, Classes, Attendance, Messages 

    -Instructors see: Dashboard, Classes, Attendance, Messages 

    -Admins see: Dashboard, User Management 

6.5.2 Logging Out 

    -Click your profile icon in the top right corner 

    -Select "Logout" 

    -You'll be redirected to the login page 

    -Always log out when using a shared computer 

6.6 Troubleshooting 

Problem: Can't log in 

    -Verify your username and password are correct 

    -Check that Caps Lock is not on 

    -Contact your administrator if the problem persists 

Problem: Can't check in to class 

    -Make sure you're enrolled in the class 

    -Verify you're not already checked into another class 

    -Check that the class session is currently active 

    -Ensure your browser allows location access (if required) 

Problem: Messages not sending 

    -Check your internet connection 

    -Refresh the page and try again 

    -Make sure the recipient exists and you have permission to message them 

Problem: Attendance records not showing 

    -Verify you've selected the correct date range or class filter 

    -Refresh the page to reload data 

    -Contact your instructor if records are still missing 